# LLM observability

- Emit one Langfuse `generation` per real model attempt (structurer or Deep Agent). Name it after the objective.
- Cache hits must not open a generation. Tokens and cost on the returned `LLMCall` stay zero.
- Use `LangfuseRun.generation()` (via `trace_llm_generation`). Do not also attach a LangChain `CallbackHandler` for the same invoke.
- Sanitize I/O through the tracer. Full payloads only when `ROUTE_AGENT_TRACE_PAYLOADS=true`.
- Failed attempts mark the observation `level=ERROR`. Langfuse failures stay fail-open.

```python
# ❌ BAD — cache hit still traces a generation
with run.generation("check_compatibility", {}):
    return cached

# ✅ GOOD
cached = cache.lookup(process, site, state)
if cached is not None:
    return mark_cache_hit(cached)
with trace_llm_generation(name=objective, model=model, metadata=meta, input_payload=payload):
    return agent.invoke(payload)
```
